this feature is for auto-recognize the captcha image so the user does not have
to type it every time. OCR runs over the network so we do not need to bundle
any native library or model file in the executable.

1. when the captcha popup opens (after step5 download captcha), the app sends
   the image to a remote OCR service and pre-fills the input field with the
   guess. the popup still opens — user is the final check.
2. while OCR is running show "Recognizing..." next to the input field. when
   the guess arrives, fill the field and select-all so user can press Enter
   to accept or just start typing to overwrite.
   important: OCR result only fills the input field. it never auto-sends.
   the user must press Send (or Enter) to submit, same as manual flow.
3. if OCR fails (network error, empty result, timeout 5s), leave the field
   empty and log it. the user types the code manually as before. no popup
   blocking.
4. captcha is case-insensitive (see feature_pop_up_wording) so the OCR result
   does not need exact case to be useful.

OCR provider: Tesseract via the network, free, no API key.
   - load tesseract.js from a CDN inside a hidden JavaFX WebView, and call
     it with the captcha image. WebKit + tesseract.js first-run download
     adds bundle size and a one-time network fetch.
   - or call a public/self-hosted Tesseract HTTP endpoint that we trust.

config: only the endpoint URL (CDN URL for tesseract.js, or REST URL of the
Tesseract HTTP service) lives in a small config file next to the jar so we
can swap providers without rebuilding. no API key.

retry-on-wrong (feature_refresh_capcha) still applies — when the user-submitted
code is wrong, the popup refreshes the image, and the OCR call runs again on
the fresh image, pre-filling again.

stop behavior (feature_stop_resume) still applies — pressing Stop during the
OCR call should cancel it; do not write fail data to the row.
